.TH "ipp-usb-api" "7" "2026-10-13" "Control API for ipp-usb"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
ipp-usb-api - Control API for \fBipp-usb\fR daemon
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBipp-usb\fR control API provides a way for local client
applications to communicate with the running \fBipp-usb\fR daemon.\&
.PP
The API uses a UNIX domain socket.\&
.PP
.SH PROTOCOL
.PP
The control API uses HTTP over a UNIX domain socket.\& Requests are
sent using the HTTP GET and POST methods.\&
.PP
The protocol is versioned independently of the \fBipp-usb\fR software
release.\& The protocol version identifies the \fBipp-usb\fR release in
which the latest protocol changes were introduced.\& It remains
unchanged across software releases that do not change the protocol.\&
.PP
The protocol is backward compatible.\& New endpoints and request
parameters may be introduced in later protocol versions without
breaking existing clients.\&
.PP
The protocol version in which each endpoint and each request or
response field was introduced is documented below.\&
.PP
.SH REQUESTS
.PP
.SS GET /status (since 0.9.22)
.PP
This is a legacy request.\& It returns a formatted status page
containing the same information as the output of the ipp-usb status
command.\&
.PP
.SS GET /version (since 0.9.35)
.PP
Returns the protocol version as a plain-text string.\&
.PP
The version identifies the \fBipp-usb\fR release in which the latest
protocol changes were introduced.\& For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
0\&.9\&.35
.fi
.RE
.PP
The returned version does not necessarily match the version of the
running ipp-usb daemon.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB/var/ipp-usb/ctrl\fR
.RS 4
\fBipp-usb\fR control socket
.PP
.RE
